  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The current sensitivity of a galvanometer can be increased by :<br />(A) decreasing the number of turns<br />(B) increasing the magnetic field<br />(C) decreasing the area of the coil<br />(D) decreasing the torsional constant of the spring</p><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "(B) and (C) only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(C) and (D) only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(A) and (C) only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(B) and (D) only",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The current in the galvanometer is calculated by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mi>&#952;</mi></math>.</p><p>Therefore, the sensitivity of the galvanometer,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, only options B and D are correct.</p></blockquote>"
  }
